.TH "RAPTOR-CONFIG" 5 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-config \- the settings of the raptor command
.SH DESCRIPTION
Settings are looked up in this order, highest first: the command line, the environment, the settings file, the model's own settings, the built\-in default. The settings file is TOML; its tables are [run], [output], [mcp] and [dev], and a key is the long name of the option without the leading dashes.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[run]
runs = 200
jobs = 4

[mcp]
port = 8765
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1), \fBraptor\-run\fR(1)
